<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>About — Nikkilog</title>
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Manrope:wght@400;500;600&family=Plus+Jakarta+Sans:wght@500;600;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Material+Symbols+Outlined:opsz,wght,FILL,GRAD@20..48,100..700,0..1,-50..200&display=block" rel="stylesheet">
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml">
    <link rel="alternate icon" href="/favicon.ico">
    <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/apple-touch-icon.png">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/tokens.css">
    <%- include('partials/meta', { metaTitle: 'About Nikkilog — what this is and why it exists', metaDescription: 'Nikkilog is a personal, non-commercial anime diary. What it is, why it exists, where the data comes from, and what it is not.' }) %>
</head>
<body>

    <%- include('partials/announcement') %>
    <%- include('partials/topbar', { active: '' }) %>

    <main class="content-area">
        <article class="content-inner prose">
            <header class="page-head">
                <span class="eyebrow">About</span>
                <h1 class="headline-lg">What this is, and why it exists</h1>
            </header>

            <p class="prose-lead">
                Nikkilog is a <strong>personal anime diary</strong> — a quiet place to keep a record of
                what you watch, rate it, and note how it made you feel. It is run by one person, as a
                hobby, and it is not a business.
            </p>

            <h2>Why it exists</h2>
            <p>
                Three honest reasons, in the order they became true.
            </p>
            <p>
                <strong>It replaced a spreadsheet.</strong> Keeping track of what you have watched, how
                far in you are, and what you thought of it, in a spreadsheet, stops working somewhere
                around the hundredth entry. This is that spreadsheet, with a proper interface.
            </p>
            <p>
                <strong>It is a learning project.</strong> Nikkilog was built to learn full-stack web
                development from scratch — the database, the server, the authentication, the design. It
                is now being deployed publicly to learn how search engines and the open web actually
                work, which is a different skill entirely and cannot be learned on localhost.
            </p>
            <p>
                <strong>It asks a question other trackers do not.</strong> Most trackers record
                <em>what</em> you watched. Nikkilog also records <em>how it felt</em> — calm, thrilling,
                emotional, nostalgic — and turns those answers into
                <a href="/mood/calm">browsable lists</a>. That data does not exist anywhere else,
                because no one else asked for it.
            </p>

            <h2>What this is not</h2>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Not a company.</strong> No ads, no paid tiers, no investors, no data sales.</li>
                <li><strong>Not affiliated with MyAnimeList</strong>, or with any anime studio, publisher or streaming service. Nothing here is endorsed by anyone.</li>
                <li><strong>Not a community site.</strong> There are no forums and no follower counts. It is one person's diary with a public face.</li>
                <li><strong>Not a streaming service.</strong> Nikkilog does not host, stream or link to video. It records what you already watched.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2 id="data">Where the data comes from</h2>
            <p>
                Being straight about this, because it matters.
            </p>
            <p>
                <strong>The catalogue is MyAnimeList's.</strong> Anime titles, alternative and Japanese
                titles, synopses, episode counts, air dates, studios, genres, scores and cover images all
                originate from <a href="https://myanimelist.net/" rel="noopener">MyAnimeList</a>. They
                remain the property of MyAnimeList and the respective rights holders. Nikkilog claims no
                ownership over any of it and does not sell it.
            </p>
            <p>
                <strong>Crediting them is not the same as being licensed by them.</strong> Saying where
                the data came from is the honest thing to do, and it is the one use of MyAnimeList's name
                their own developer agreement permits. It does not, by itself, grant permission to
                republish their content — that is a separate question, and this project does not claim to
                have resolved it.
            </p>
            <p>
                <strong>If you hold rights to something shown here and want it removed, it will be</strong> —
                no argument, no form to fill in. See <a href="#contact">contact</a> below.
            </p>
            <p>
                <strong>The mood data is ours.</strong> The answers to "how did this feel?" were given by
                people using Nikkilog. They were not copied from anywhere, because there is nowhere to
                copy them from. That is the part of this site that is genuinely original.
            </p>

            <h2>How it is built</h2>
            <p>
                Node.js, Express, EJS and MySQL, rendered on the server. The source is on GitHub and the
                design, the browser extension and the mood layer are all described in the repository.
                No trackers, no analytics scripts, no third-party fonts beyond Google Fonts.
            </p>

            <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
            <% if (contact) { %>
            <p>
                For anything at all — a correction, a removal request, a bug, or just to say hello:
                <a href="<%= contact.url %>" rel="me noopener" target="_blank"><%= contact.display %></a> on <%= contact.network %>.
                A direct message is the fastest way to reach me.
            </p>
            <% } else { %>
            <p class="muted">
                No contact details have been configured for this instance yet.
            </p>
            <% } %>
            <p class="muted">
                This page is not legal advice and makes no legal claim. It is a plain description of
                what this project is, written so that anyone can see exactly what they are looking at.
            </p>
        </article>
    </main>

    <%- include('partials/footer') %>

    <script src="/js/topbar.js" defer></script>
    <script src="/js/promos.js" defer></script>
</body>
</html>
